{
  "comment": "Brief 31-3, 3b (ii) after Codex on #834: command strings the solo lead's shell refuses and ones it runs. Read by pi/test/team.test.ts (the extension) and internal/cli/team_confirm_test.go (the guard's second layer), so the two layers read the same forms. amq_squad_allowlist is the read-only amq-squad verbs the solo lead's shell may run; every other amq-squad verb (bare amq-squad included) is refused, since before the yes no lead lock is held.",
  "refused": [
    "t\"\"mux send-keys -t %7 \"/squad confirm 0123456789abcdef\" Enter",
    "t\\mux ls",
    "$'tmux' ls",
    "\"tm\"'ux' ls",
    "TMUX ls",
    "/opt/homebrew/bin/t''mux list-panes",
    "ls; /opt/homebrew/bin/tmux list-panes",
    "echo x | tmux load-buffer -",
    "tm${x}ux send-keys -t %7 x Enter",
    "tm$(true)ux send-keys -t %7 x Enter",
    "`echo tm`ux send-keys",
    "eval \"$(printf 't%smux' '') send-keys -t %7 x Enter\"",
    "exec -a ls ./t_m_u_x send-keys",
    "env -S \"t_m_u_x send-keys -t %7 x Enter\"",
    "a''mq-squad te''am confirm sha256:x@absent",
    "amq\\-squad team apply --digest sha256:x@absent",
    "sh -c 'amq-squad team confirm sha256:x@absent'",
    "(cd /tmp && amq-squad team apply --digest sha256:x@absent)",
    "amq-squad up",
    "amq-squad lead --team",
    "amq-squad scheduler run --project .",
    "amq-squad launch",
    "amq-squad team apply --digest sha256:x@absent",
    "amq-squad task reset t1",
    "amq-squad",
    "sh -c 'amq-squad up --skip-install'",
    "env A=1 /usr/local/bin/amq-squad lead"
  ],
  "runs": [
    "echo \"hello world\"",
    "git log --format=\"%h %s\" -3",
    "ls -la",
    "go test ./...",
    "amq-squad status --json",
    "amq-squad task list --json",
    "cd $HOME/code && make build",
    "grep -rn \"func main\" .",
    "echo the team will apply soon",
    "amq-squad task show t1 --json",
    "amq-squad team propose --from plan.json --project .",
    "amq-squad doctor --json",
    "amq-squad version",
    "amq-squad context --json"
  ],
  "amq_squad_allowlist": [
    "status",
    "context",
    "doctor",
    "version",
    "task show",
    "task list",
    "team propose"
  ]
}
